<node id="&quot;CYTOSOL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The liquid portion of the cytoplasm where many metabolic reactions take place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The liquid portion of the cytoplasm, serving as a medium for various biochemical reactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLATHRIN-MEDIATED_ENDOCYTOSIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clathrin-mediated endocytosis is a process by which cells internalize extracellular material through clathrin-coated vesicles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EPHB-MEDIATED_FORWARD_SIGNALING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"EPHB-mediated forward signaling refers to cellular signaling processes initiated by EPHB receptors, typically involved in cell-cell communication and development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ERBB1_DOWNSTREAM_SIGNALING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ErbB1 downstream signaling involves the activation of pathways triggered by the ErbB1 receptor, often associated with growth factor signaling and cellular responses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RHO_GTPASES_ACTIVATE_WASPS_AND_WAVES.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"RHO GTPases activate WASP (Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein) and WAVE (WASP family verprolin-homologous proteins), which are involved in actin cytoskeleton remodeling."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PDGFR-BETA_SIGNALING_PATHWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The PDGFR-beta signaling pathway is activated by platelet-derived growth factor (PDGF) binding to its receptor PDGFR-beta, leading to various cellular responses such as proliferation and differentiation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PATHOGENIC_ESCHERICHIA_COLI_INFECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pathogenic Escherichia coli infection refers to the process by which E. coli causes disease in a host organism."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENZYME_BINDING.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enzyme binding refers to the interaction of proteins with enzymes, often to regulate enzymatic activity or participate in biochemical pathways."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENDOSOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A membrane-bound organelle involved in sorting and processing proteins and lipids for recycling or degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"A membrane-bound organelle involved in the sorting and processing of proteins and lipids."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIN_CYTOSKELETON.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The actin cytoskeleton is a network of actin filaments that provides structural support and enables cell movement, shape maintenance, and other cellular functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR EXOSOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extracellular vesicles released by cells, containing various biomolecules for intercellular communication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Small vesicles released by cells into the extracellular space, containing biomolecules like proteins and RNA."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CELL_PROJECTION.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cell projections are extensions of the cell membrane and cytoplasm, such as filopodia or lamellipodia, which are involved in cell migration and sensing the environment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR REGION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The space outside of cells where intercellular communication and other processes occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The space outside the cell where extracellular processes occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FICOLIN-1-RICH GRANULE LUMEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A compartment within granules rich in ficolin-1, a protein involved in innate immunity."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specialized compartment within granules rich in ficolin-1, a protein involved in innate immune responses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FOCAL ADHESION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Structures that connect the actin cytoskeleton to the extracellular matrix, enabling cell adhesion and migration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Structures that link the actin cytoskeleton to the extracellular matrix, facilitating cell adhesion and migration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROTEIN-MACROMOLECULE_ADAPTOR_ACTIVITY.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Protein-macromolecule adaptor activity involves proteins that facilitate interactions between different macromolecules, such as proteins and nucleic acids."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CELL PROJECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Projections from the cell membrane, such as filopodia or lamellipodia, involved in movement and sensing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protrusions from the cell membrane, such as lamellipodia or filopodia, involved in movement and sensing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROWTH CONE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A dynamic structure at the tip of growing axons that senses guidance cues during neuronal development."&lt;SEP&gt;"A structure at the tip of growing axons involved in detecting guidance cues during neuronal development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYTOPLASM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The gel-like substance inside the cell where many biochemical processes occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"The jelly-like substance inside the cell, excluding the nucleus, where many cellular processes occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYTOSOL.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The cytosol is the fluid-filled space inside a cell, excluding the organelles, where various biochemical reactions occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LAMELLIPODIUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A sheet-like protrusion at the leading edge of migrating cells, driven by actin polymerization and involved in cell movement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A sheet-like protrusion at the leading edge of migrating cells, driven by actin polymerization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NUCLEUS.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The nucleus is the membrane-bound organelle in eukaryotic cells that contains most of the cell's genetic material."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEURON PROJECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extensions of neurons, such as axons and dendrites, that facilitate communication between neurons."&lt;SEP&gt;"Projections from neurons, such as dendrites and axons, involved in communication with other neurons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYTOSKELETON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A dynamic network of protein filaments that maintains cell shape, facilitates movement, and organizes cellular components."&lt;SEP&gt;"A network of protein filaments that maintains cell shape, enables movement, and organizes the cell's components."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR_EXOSOME.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extracellular exosomes are vesicles released by cells into the extracellular space, often containing proteins, RNA, or other molecules for intercellular communication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NUCLEUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The membrane-bound organelle containing the cell's genetic material and regulating gene expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"The membrane-bound organelle containing the cell's genetic material."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIN CYTOSKELETON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A structural network within the cell composed of actin filaments that provides shape and support."&lt;SEP&gt;"The network of actin filaments that provides structural support to the cell."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE_OF_DOUBLE-STRAND_BREAK.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A site of double-strand break refers to a location within DNA where both strands are broken, requiring repair mechanisms such as homologous recombination or non-homologous end joining."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECRETORY GRANULE LUMEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The interior space of secretory granules where molecules are stored before secretion."&lt;SEP&gt;"The interior space of secretory granules, where molecules are stored prior to secretion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACTIN_FILAMENT_BINDING.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Actin filament binding refers to the ability of proteins to bind and interact with actin filaments in the cytoskeleton."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARPC5&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ARPC5 is a protein involved in cellular processes including actin filament binding, nucleation, and regulation of actin dynamics. It participates in signaling events such as CDC42 signaling, Clathrin-mediated endocytosis, EPHB- and ErbB1 downstream signaling, PDGFR-beta signaling, neutrophil degranulation, and others."&lt;SEP&gt;"ARPC5 is a protein involved in various cellular structures and processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATION_OF_ACTIN_DYNAMICS_FOR_PHAGOCYTIC_CUP_FORMATION.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The regulation of actin dynamics for phagocytic cup formation is a process by which cells engulf particles or pathogens, involving the reorganization of the actin cytoskeleton."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RAC1_SIGNALING_PATHWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The RAC1 signaling pathway involves the small GTPase RAC1, which plays roles in cytoskeletal organization, cell migration, and other cellular processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARP2/3 PROTEIN COMPLEX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A protein complex involved in actin polymerization and cytoskeleton organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arp2/3 protein complex is a key player in actin polymerization and cytoskeleton organization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SITE OF DOUBLE-STRAND BREAK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A location within the cell where both strands of the DNA double helix have been broken, often during DNA repair processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"A location within the cell where breaks in both strands of DNA occur, often during repair processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4721c0e5a5d6f31a4758abea9e3bb66a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PDGFR-BETA_SIGNALING_PATHWAY.&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
  <data key="d1">"ARPC5 participates in the PDGFR-beta signaling pathway, indicating its role in cell proliferation and differentiation."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARPC4&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e</data>
  <data key="d1">"ARPC4 is involved in processes related to pathogenic E. coli infection, suggesting its role in host defense or bacterial invasion."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
